  m_text: 'The Tibetan alphabet, known as Salje Sumchu, has a rich history intertwined
    with the culture and spirituality of Tibet. This unique script, developed in
    the 7th century, was inspired by the Indian Brahmi script and has evolved over
    the centuries. The story of Salje Sumchu is not just about letters; it reflects
    the journey of Tibetan identity and the preservation of its language and literature.
    Each character carries a deep significance, representing not only sounds but
    also the essence of Tibetan philosophy and tradition.

